{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-83618:  libsoup3 security update (IMPORTANT)",
  "Description": "[3.6.5-20]\n- CVE-2026-102557 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket\n  message reassembly\n\n[3.6.5-19]\n- CVE-2026-102556 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow from WebSocket\n  Pong signal type confusion\n\n[3.6.5-18]\n- CVE-2026-102558 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket\n  receive-buffer growth\n\n[3.6.5-17]\n- CVE-2026-102555 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow via uninitialized\n  length in data-URI base64 decoding\n\n[3.6.5-16]\n- CVE-2026-102560 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during outgoing\n  permessage-deflate buffer growth\n\n[3.6.5-15]\n- CVE-2026-102559 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket\n  client-frame masking\n\n[3.6.5-14]\n- Fix CVE-2026-85197: http2 crash after connection destroyed\n\n[3.6.5-13]\n- Fix CVE-2026-15711: Reject oversized WebSocket control frames\n\n[3.6.5-12]\n- Fix CVE-2026-15709: bound decompressed WebSocket message size\n\n[3.6.5-11]\n- Add patches for CVE-2026-4271 and CVE-2026-5119",
